    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2309-5068> ;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/rightsHolder> <urn:uuid:4cdd2ad4-9f4b-4923-b5b5-b48fc94cccfb> , <urn:uuid:c2c98445-9dac-4515-bd06-ce6c5bdace11> , <urn:uuid:6387b30f-8473-4fe0-b8d5-6f4257c1e25f> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/annotation#markdownDescription>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/annotation#> ;
    annotation:markdownDescription """
Use this annotation on an ontology, class, property, or individual for
explanations that benefit from Markdown: scope, examples, modeling decisions,
ownership rules, and application behavior. Use an English language tag for the
English explanation. Keep a short definition in `rdfs:comment` where useful.

Markdown can include headings, lists, tables, fenced code examples, and links.
Consumers render this description when present and use `rdfs:comment` when it
is absent.

An explanation is an annotation. Describing a subclass relationship, a property
range, a SHACL constraint, or an application default does not implement it.
Identify agreed changes awaiting implementation explicitly, so readers can
distinguish the recorded decision from the current axioms.
"""@en .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/annotation#subtitle>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/annotation#> .

<https://ekgf.org/ontology/annotation#summary>
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ekgf.org/ontology/annotation#> .
